<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal Telecom profit up 51 pct.</title>
<headline>Portugal Telecom profit up 51 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31</p>
<p>(In billions of escudos unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit	     54.92     vs     36.25</p>
<p>    Gross div		  138 escudos  vs   91 escudos</p>
<p>    Earnings per share     289 escudos  vs  191 escudos</p>
<p>    Cons operating revenue   477.83     vs  429.18</p>
<p>    Operating costs	    350.27     vs  321.11</p>
<p>    Cashflow		     172.61     vs  156.12</p>
<p>    Net debt			31.6	vs   39.4</p>
<p>Note - Company name is Portugal Telecom  </p>
<p>    Income before tax	  103.20     vs   79.77</p>
<p>Depreciation and</p>
<p>    ammortisation		108.11     vs   98.89</p>
<p>    EBITDA			 237.77     vs  211.47</p>
<p>    Investment		   122.13     vs  115.98</p>
<p>    Overall operating margin  26.7	vs   25.2</p>
<p>    Return on equity	     14	 vs    10</p>
<p>    Return on sales	     11.5	vs    8.5</p>
<p>    Employees per 1,000 lines  5.1	vs    5.6</p>
